511	/**
512	 * Matches Docker's own, specific "no such volume" error line (confirmed
513	 * against the real CLI: `docker volume inspect <missing-name>` exits 1
514	 * with stderr `Error response from daemon: get <name>: no such volume`).
515	 * This is the ONLY signal `inspectVolume` treats as genuine absence —
516	 * exported so the classification itself can be unit-tested with
517	 * synthetic stderr text, without a real Docker daemon. Every other
518	 * nonzero-exit stderr (a daemon unreachable error, a permission
519	 * failure, or anything else) does NOT match, so it is treated as a real
520	 * failure by `inspectVolume`, never as absence.
521	 */
