1162	 * as `0.0.0.0`), and never IPv6 loopback `"::1"` either, since this
1163	 * stack's own published services are always configured with the literal
1164	 * IPv4 loopback address (see docker-compose.yml) — accepting `::1` here
1165	 * too would let a silent IPv6-wildcard regression (`::`, which Linux can
1166	 * map to dual-stack `0.0.0.0`-like exposure) pass unnoticed.
1167	 *
1168	 * Pure and synchronous — independently unit-testable with synthetic
1169	 * values, no Docker required. Used to validate BOTH the static resolved
1170	 * configuration (`resolveComposePublishedPorts`) and real running
1171	 * containers' bindings (`getContainerHostPortBindings`).
1172	 */
